Proposal (lane RELEASE, the brief's step 4): a longer gate limit for one test file.

Not applied: tools/ci_gate.py and tools/ are frozen; only Lucas applies this, by his
hand or his word. Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check tools/release/proposals/ci-gate-publish-timeout.patch
    git apply tools/release/proposals/ci-gate-publish-timeout.patch

Why: lane A7 found tools/test_claude_fixer_publish.py passing the gate's 180 s limit
on two hosted macOS jobs (macos-26-arm64) and taking 97.6 s and 128.4 s on two
passing ones. CSL-495 keeps that file, so the retirement patch does not remove it.
Hosted macOS logs show only dots for it, so no per-test macOS timing exists yet;
tools/release/timings.py prints one when run there. On Linux (lane RELEASE, Nov 14,
2026, python 3.12 and 3.14t) it takes 29 to 31 s, of which one wiring test takes
10 s; with retire-review-workflows.patch applied it takes 19 to 20 s.

What it does:
- tools/ci_gate.py: FILE_TIMEOUTS gives tools/test_claude_fixer_publish.py 300 s
  (lane A7's suggestion); every other file keeps RUN_TIMEOUT (180 s).
- tools/test_ci_gate.py: FileTimeoutTests, which fails if a FILE_TIMEOUTS entry names
  a file the gate does not run, lowers a limit, or is not passed by run_suite.

Blank context lines are written as empty lines, which git apply accepts; the file
then has no trailing whitespace for the gate's whitespace check.

diff --git a/tools/ci_gate.py b/tools/ci_gate.py
index c98bd2f30d3e5956df17def69a7c1aebc57d9776..07430adcd74a3d4c9313488b62a72cae7b3e0276 100644
--- a/tools/ci_gate.py
+++ b/tools/ci_gate.py
@@ -32,6 +32,11 @@ ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
 ZERO_SHA = "0" * 40
 GIT = ["git", "-c", "core.longpaths=true", "-c", "core.quotePath=false"]
 RUN_TIMEOUT = 180
+# Test files allowed longer than RUN_TIMEOUT, each with the measurement behind it.
+# tools/test_claude_fixer_publish.py: 97.6 s and 128.4 s on passing macos-26-arm64 jobs and
+# over 180 s on two others (lane A7, Nov 12, 2026); 29 to 31 s on Linux, where one test
+# takes 10 s of it (lane RELEASE, Nov 14, 2026, tools/release/timings.py).
+FILE_TIMEOUTS = {"tools/test_claude_fixer_publish.py": 300}

 # Paths that can break the provider-free gate. Only logged since CSL-376.
 GATE_PREFIXES = (
@@ -434,7 +439,7 @@ def run_suite() -> None:
         else:
             run_program(list(program))
     for program in extra_suite_programs(tests):
-        run_test_file(program[0])
+        run_test_file(program[0], timeout=FILE_TIMEOUTS.get(program[0], RUN_TIMEOUT))
     print("CI_GATE_PASS provider_calls=0 scientific_admission=false", flush=True)


diff --git a/tools/test_ci_gate.py b/tools/test_ci_gate.py
index 7ac146d42d6ed75ebafeb68b83eef2fcafd34496..d9dc165804b647364bab34e5e2f1afa9ec696a1c 100644
